// yel's standard library, written in yel over the prelude's externs (runtime/prelude.yel). This
// directory, runtime/std/core, is its core: what the language needs (what the compiler lowers
// syntax to, the methods of its own types), and every program reaches its names without an include,
// after its own and the prelude's: a program naming a func as one here names its own. Its folders
// are one package, a file for each part: text (text, char, buffer, format), collections (list, map,
// set, option), numbers (number, integer), async (async, streams), reactive (observe, reactive,
// view-events), runtime (memory, value, assert), host (WASI natively: host-*.yel, cli-exit). The
// rest of the library is a package in each other directory of runtime/std, reached only by an
// include of std:<name> (std:encoding/json); a std:<name> with no directory is WASI's wasi:<name>
// (std:cli, std:filesystem), natively core's host.

package yel:std@0.1.0;
